# DreamNexa frontend — environment variables
# Copy this file to .env (and .env.production for prod builds) and fill in real values.
# All Vite env vars must be prefixed with VITE_ to be exposed to the browser bundle.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
VITE_SOCKET_URL=

# ── Google AdSense ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave these blank until Google approves your site. While blank, AdBanner
# automatically falls back to the existing house/promo creative instead of
# showing an empty box — nothing breaks before or during the review.
#
# 1) VITE_ADSENSE_CLIENT — your publisher ID, format "ca-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"
#    (find it in AdSense > Account > Account information).
# 2) VITE_ADSENSE_SLOT_TOP / _INLINE / _SIDEBAR — the numeric ad unit slot ID
#    for each ad unit you create in AdSense > Ads > By ad unit > Display ads.
#    Create one unit per position (a horizontal/banner unit for "top", a
#    rectangle/in-article unit for "inline", a vertical unit for "sidebar")
#    and paste each unit's data-ad-slot value here.
VITE_ADSENSE_CLIENT=
VITE_ADSENSE_SLOT_TOP=
VITE_ADSENSE_SLOT_INLINE=
VITE_ADSENSE_SLOT_SIDEBAR=
